# The build context is the repo root (every service needs the Commons sibling module), so without
# this file Docker would upload the entire tree — including ShopifyApp's 23k vendored files and
# every UI's node_modules — to the daemon on every build.

# Never send secrets to the build daemon. Keystores hold PRIVATE keys; they come from Secrets
# Manager at runtime and are never baked into an image.
*.p12
*.jks
# ...except the truststore, which is re-admitted deliberately. It contains only the DAO's PUBLIC
# certificate (docs/keystore-rotation.md: "Only the public certificate goes in the truststore"),
# it is committed for that reason, and the BFF loads it from `classpath:dao-truststore.p12`.
# Excluding it would leave the BFF image with no truststore, and BFF -> DAO TLS verification would
# fail closed at the first call — the negation keeps the blanket rule above safe without breaking
# the one file the rule was never meant to catch.
!**/dao-truststore.p12
!**/*truststore*.jks
.env
**/application-local.properties
**/oauthclient.txt

# Build outputs. These are rebuilt inside the image; copying host artifacts in would make the
# image depend on whatever happened to be on the machine that built it.
**/target/
**/dist/
**/node_modules/

# Deferred Shopify scaffold — a separate repository, and nothing here builds from it.
ShopifyApp/

# Local runtime noise
*.log
logs/
snapshots/
asset-store/
tests/e2e/artifacts/
tests/e2e/node_modules/
*.mp4

# VCS and tooling
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
